Two events are **mutually exclusive** if no outcome belongs to both, so $A \cap B = \varnothing$ and their circles do not overlap.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,4.6);
\draw (2.1,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw (5.9,2.3) circle (1.7);
\node[anchor=north west, font=\small] at (0.15,4.5) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.0,4.15) {$A$};
\node at (7.0,4.15) {$B$};
\node[font=\small] at (4,-0.55) {mutually exclusive: no overlap};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two events are **non-mutually exclusive** if at least one outcome belongs to both, so their circles overlap.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,4.6);
\draw (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\node[anchor=north west, font=\small] at (0.15,4.5) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.9,4.15) {$A$};
\node at (6.1,4.15) {$B$};
\node[font=\small] at (4,-0.55) {non-mutually exclusive: circles overlap};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

'**Inclusive or**' ('$A$ or $B$, or both') means at least one happens, counting the overlap once.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\fill[gray!35] (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,4.6);
\draw (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\node[anchor=north west, font=\small] at (0.15,4.5) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.9,4.15) {$A$};
\node at (6.1,4.15) {$B$};
\node[font=\small] at (4,-0.55) {inclusive or: overlap shaded};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

'**Exclusive or**' ('$A$ or $B$, but not both') means exactly one happens, so the overlap is removed.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\fill[gray!35] (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\begin{scope}
\clip (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\fill[white] (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\end{scope}
\draw (0,0) rectangle (8,4.6);
\draw (3,2.3) circle (1.7);
\draw (5,2.3) circle (1.7);
\node[anchor=north west, font=\small] at (0.15,4.5) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.9,4.15) {$A$};
\node at (6.1,4.15) {$B$};
\node[font=\small] at (4,-0.55) {exclusive or: overlap not shaded};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

